      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T17:32:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "iommu_coherency() actually checks page table coherency, while here we are dealing with a context table, not a page table. So we should use ecap_coherent() instead (like the host driver\u0027s __iommu_flush_cache() does)?\n\nVT-d spec about ecap_coherent(): \"This field indicates if hardware access to the root, scalable-mode root, context, scalable-mode-context, scalable-mode PASIDdirectory, scalable-mode PASID-table, and interrupt-remap tables, and legacy-mode second-stage paging structures are coherent (snooped) or not.\" - i.e. when it comes to root, context and PASID tables (not page tables), it is for both legacy and scalable modes. Whereas ecap_smpwc() is for page tables only, thus shouldn\u0027t be used here.\n\n...BTW regarding iommu_coherency(), in the future (e.g. in 6.18) we\u0027d better reuse the host driver\u0027s iommu_paging_structure_coherency() helper (moving it to a header) instead of introducing our own one. (And maybe similarly for various other helpers.)",
      "revId": "c7ec47177158bdc7e2f56e23dc9f5ca6c8b2d929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
